{"id":"q1-09-s1","title":"Storage and recovery","scopeHtml":"<p>Scope: pages and heap, buffer pool, WAL, checkpoints, crash recovery, vacuum and bloat, sizing. Questions are still to be written.</p>","notes":[{"id":"pages-and-the-heap","title":"Pages and the heap","html":"<p><strong>Postgres stores a table as a file of fixed 8 KB pages; rows (tuples) are packed into pages in no particular order. This unordered file is the \"heap\".</strong> Disk and memory both move whole pages, so the page is the unit of I/O.</p>\n<p>Page layout:</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>8192-byte page</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>+-------------------------------+</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>| page header (24 B)            |</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>| line pointers: lp1 lp2 lp3 -> |  (4 B each, grow downward)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>|           free space          |</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>| &#x3C;- tuple3 tuple2 tuple1       |  (tuples grow upward from the end)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>| special space (indexes only)  |</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>+-------------------------------+</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Tuple header: ~23 B (xmin, xmax, ctid, infomask) + null bitmap + data</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>A row's physical address is <code>ctid = (page number, line pointer index)</code>, e.g. <code>(120, 3)</code>. Indexes store ctids. A <strong>line pointer</strong> indirection lets Postgres move a tuple within a page (compaction) without changing its ctid.</p>\n<p>Large values (over about 2 KB) are compressed and/or moved to a side TOAST table, so a row with a 1 MB <code>text</code> stays small in the heap.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 801.2 68\" width=\"801.2\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Index points at ctid; ctid points to page and slot in the heap\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M115.2 34 L171.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M115.2 34 L171.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;0.201;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M288.8 34 L344.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M288.8 34 L344.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;0.401;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M462.40000000000003 34 L518.4000000000001 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M462.40000000000003 34 L518.4000000000001 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;0.601;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M643.2 34 L699.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M643.2 34 L699.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;0.801;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"63.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Index entry</text><rect x=\"171.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"230\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">ctid (120, 3)</text><rect x=\"344.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"403.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Heap page 120</text><rect x=\"518.4000000000001\" y=\"12\" width=\"124.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"580.8000000000001\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Line pointer 3</text><rect x=\"699.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"744.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Tuple</text></svg><figcaption>Index points at ctid; ctid points to page and slot in the heap</figcaption></figure>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">SELECT</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> pg_relation_size(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">'users'</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)            </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">AS</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> heap_bytes,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">       pg_total_relation_size(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">'users'</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)       </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">AS</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> with_indexes_toast,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">       pg_relation_filepath(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">'users'</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">-- inspect pages: CREATE EXTENSION pageinspect;</span></span></code></pre>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> 50M rows x 100 B data + 24 B header + 4 B pointer = about 130 B each. 8192 B / 130 B is roughly 60 rows per page, so about 830,000 pages = 6.7 GB heap. A sequential scan reads 6.7 GB; at 1 GB/s that is ~7 s (illustrative).</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> InnoDB uses 16 KB pages and stores rows in the primary-key B+tree (clustered), so secondary lookups cost two tree walks. Postgres's heap means every index is \"secondary\"; <code>CLUSTER</code> reorders once but does not maintain order.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> Page size is fixed at compile time (8 KB default); effectively one-way. Fillfactor per table is changeable and trades space for room for HOT updates.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A filing room of identical folders (pages), each holding many sheets (rows) in whatever order they arrived, with an index card box that says which folder and which slot.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Believing Postgres tables are ordered by primary key.</li>\n<li>Forgetting TOAST when estimating row size.</li>\n<li>Ignoring that every row has ~24 B overhead; narrow tables with tiny columns are dominated by it.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"buffer-pool-and-the-os-cache","title":"Buffer pool and the OS cache","html":"<p><strong>The buffer pool (<code>shared_buffers</code>) is Postgres's own cache of pages in RAM.</strong> A query asks for page N; if it is in shared buffers (hit) it is read from RAM, else it is read from disk (miss) into a buffer, evicting another via a clock-sweep algorithm. Pages modified in memory are \"dirty\" until written.</p>\n<p>Postgres also relies on the <strong>OS page cache</strong> (double buffering): a miss in shared_buffers may still be a fast read from the OS cache.</p>\n<p>Typical config for a 64 GB server:</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>shared_buffers = 16GB           # ~25% of RAM is the common start</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>effective_cache_size = 48GB     # planner hint: shared_buffers + OS cache</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>work_mem = 32MB                 # per sort/hash NODE per query, not per connection</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>maintenance_work_mem = 2GB      # VACUUM, CREATE INDEX</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Check hit ratio:</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">SELECT</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> sum</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(blks_hit)::</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">float</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> /</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> nullif</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">sum</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(blks_hit)</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">+</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">sum</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(blks_read),</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">0</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">) </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">AS</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> hit_ratio</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">FROM</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> pg_stat_database;   </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">-- OLTP target: above 0.99</span></span></code></pre>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 614.4000000000001 68\" width=\"614.4000000000001\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Read path: buffer pool, else OS cache, else disk\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M282.8 34 L338.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M282.8 34 L338.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M456.40000000000003 34 L512.4000000000001 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M456.40000000000003 34 L512.4000000000001 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Query</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"124.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"220.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">shared_buffers</text><rect x=\"338.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"397.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">OS page cache</text><rect x=\"512.4000000000001\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"557.4000000000001\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Disk</text></svg><figcaption>Read path: buffer pool, else OS cache, else disk</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> Working set (hot data plus indexes) is 30 GB, RAM 64 GB, shared_buffers 16 GB: most reads hit shared_buffers or the OS cache, a few ms of random disk reads for cold pages. If the working set grows to 200 GB, hit ratio drops, <code>iowait</code> rises, p99 latency spikes: the signal to add RAM, partition, or add read replicas.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Some teams run huge <code>shared_buffers</code> (up to 40%) on dedicated boxes; others keep it small and let the OS cache work. Amazon Aurora replaced the storage layer entirely, pushing WAL replay down to storage nodes.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Books on your desk (shared_buffers), on the shelf in the same room (OS cache), and in the warehouse across town (disk).</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Setting <code>work_mem</code> high and multiplying by many connections (out of memory): it applies per sort/hash node.</li>\n<li>Believing shared_buffers should be 80% of RAM.</li>\n<li>Not knowing that <code>EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)</code> shows <code>shared hit</code> vs <code>read</code>.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"write-ahead-log-wal","title":"Write-ahead log (WAL)","html":"<p><strong>The WAL is an append-only log where every change is recorded BEFORE the data page is changed on disk.</strong> This rule (\"write-ahead\") is what makes crash recovery possible and durability cheap: appending to a log is one sequential write, while flushing the many scattered dirty data pages randomly would be slow.</p>\n<p>Flow of an UPDATE:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Change the page in shared_buffers (mark dirty).</li>\n<li>Append a WAL record (a description of the change) to the WAL buffer, tagged with an LSN (log sequence number: a byte position in the log).</li>\n<li>At COMMIT, flush WAL up to that LSN with fsync, then acknowledge.</li>\n<li>Dirty data pages are written later by the background writer or a checkpoint.</li>\n</ol>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 970 68\" width=\"970\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Log first, data later: commit only needs the sequential WAL flush\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.167;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.167;0.168;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M326 34 L382 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M326 34 L382 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.167;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.167;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M478 34 L534 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M478 34 L534 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M624 34 L680 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M624 34 L680 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M770 34 L826 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M770 34 L826 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.667;0.833;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4.800000000000001s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.667;0.833;0.834;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">UPDATE</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"168\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"242\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Dirty page in memory</text><rect x=\"382\" y=\"12\" width=\"96\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"430\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">WAL record</text><rect x=\"534\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"579\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">fsync WAL</text><rect x=\"680\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"725\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">COMMIT ok</text><rect x=\"826\" y=\"12\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"892\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Data file later</text></svg><figcaption>Log first, data later: commit only needs the sequential WAL flush</figcaption></figure>\n<p>WAL files are 16 MB segments in <code>pg_wal/</code>. Key settings:</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>wal_level = replica          # 'logical' adds info for logical replication/CDC</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>max_wal_size = 8GB           # soft cap that triggers checkpoints</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>min_wal_size = 1GB</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>wal_compression = on         # smaller full-page images</span></span></code></pre>\n<p><strong>Full-page writes.</strong> The first change to a page after a checkpoint writes the whole 8 KB page image into WAL, protecting against torn pages (a crash during an 8 KB write when the OS writes 4 KB blocks). This is why WAL volume spikes right after each checkpoint.</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> 5,000 updates/s, ~300 B of WAL each (more after checkpoints with full pages) is roughly 1.5 MB/s steady, about 130 GB/day. If you archive WAL for backups (file 10) that is your storage and network cost.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> The same log ships to replicas (streaming replication), feeds CDC tools (Debezium with logical decoding) and enables point-in-time recovery. Kafka's commit log and LSM stores' write-ahead logs follow the same principle.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A ship's logbook: write each action in the book first. If the crew forgets the state of the ship after a storm, replaying the book rebuilds it.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Saying WAL stores the changed pages. It stores change descriptions (plus occasional full-page images).</li>\n<li>Forgetting that a stuck replication slot prevents WAL deletion and can fill the disk.</li>\n<li>Confusing WAL (recovery log) with the commit log <code>pg_xact</code> (transaction status).</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"checkpoints","title":"Checkpoints","html":"<p><strong>A checkpoint forces all dirty pages up to a certain point in the WAL out to the data files, so recovery only needs to replay WAL AFTER that point.</strong> It writes a checkpoint record containing the redo start LSN.</p>\n<p>Triggers: every <code>checkpoint_timeout</code> (default 5 min) or when WAL since the last checkpoint approaches <code>max_wal_size</code>. To avoid an I/O burst, writing is spread over <code>checkpoint_completion_target</code> (default 0.9 of the interval).</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>checkpoint_timeout = 15min</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>checkpoint_completion_target = 0.9</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>max_wal_size = 16GB</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>log_checkpoints = on        # watch \"checkpoints timed\" vs \"requested\"</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Trade-off:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Checkpoint interval</th>\n<th>Pros</th>\n<th>Cons</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Frequent (1 to 5 min)</td>\n<td>Fast crash recovery</td>\n<td>More I/O, more full-page WAL</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Rare (15 to 30 min)</td>\n<td>Smoother I/O, less WAL</td>\n<td>Longer crash recovery (replay up to the interval's WAL)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 799.2 68\" width=\"799.2\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Checkpoint bounds how much WAL recovery must replay\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M115.2 34 L171.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M115.2 34 L171.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M310.4 34 L366.4 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M310.4 34 L366.4 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M563.2 34 L619.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M563.2 34 L619.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"63.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Dirty pages</text><rect x=\"171.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"240.79999999999998\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Checkpoint flush</text><rect x=\"366.4\" y=\"12\" width=\"196.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"464.79999999999995\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Checkpoint record in WAL</text><rect x=\"619.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"168\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"703.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Recovery starts here</text></svg><figcaption>Checkpoint bounds how much WAL recovery must replay</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Incident pattern.</strong> Latency spikes every 5 minutes on the dot with <code>max_wal_size</code> too small: checkpoints are \"requested\" (not timed), I/O saturates. Metric: <code>pg_stat_bgwriter</code> / <code>pg_stat_checkpointer</code> ratio of requested to timed checkpoints; fix by raising <code>max_wal_size</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> WAL generation 20 MB/s; replay rate maybe 100+ MB/s; with <code>checkpoint_timeout = 15min</code> you may have up to 18 GB of WAL to replay in a crash: about 3 minutes of recovery plus startup (numbers illustrative).</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Saving your game: after a save, a crash only costs you the play since the save, not the whole run.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Saying a checkpoint is what makes a commit durable. WAL fsync does that.</li>\n<li>Setting very frequent checkpoints \"for safety\" and causing I/O storms.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"crash-recovery","title":"Crash recovery","html":"<p><strong>After a crash, Postgres starts, finds the last checkpoint's redo point and replays every WAL record after it, bringing data files to the exact state at the crash.</strong> Uncommitted transactions need no undo: their rows are invisible because their xids never got committed in <code>pg_xact</code>.</p>\n<p>Steps:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Read <code>pg_control</code> to find the latest checkpoint.</li>\n<li>Replay WAL forward from the redo LSN (redo is idempotent: each page stores the LSN of its last change; replay applies a record only if the page LSN is older).</li>\n<li>End of valid WAL reached: database opens. In-flight transactions are treated as aborted.</li>\n</ol>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 728.4 68\" width=\"728.4\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Recovery is redo only: replay from last checkpoint, no undo pass\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M290 34 L346 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M290 34 L346 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M542.8 34 L598.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M542.8 34 L598.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Crash</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"224\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Read pg_control</text><rect x=\"346\" y=\"12\" width=\"196.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"444.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Replay WAL from redo LSN</text><rect x=\"598.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"657.5999999999999\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Open database</text></svg><figcaption>Recovery is redo only: replay from last checkpoint, no undo pass</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Check progress in the log: <code>redo starts at 3A/1C000028</code>, <code>redo done at ...</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Contrast.</strong> Systems with ARIES-style recovery (InnoDB, SQL Server, Oracle) have analysis, redo and UNDO phases because they modify pages in place. Postgres skips undo by design, at the price of vacuum.</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> Power failure while 200 transactions run. 120 had COMMIT acknowledged (their WAL was fsynced): they survive. The 80 that had not committed vanish. No data file can be half-applied because WAL replay plus full-page images fix torn pages.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Managed services (RDS, Cloud SQL) restart a crashed instance and rely on exactly this; Aurora recovers in seconds because storage does redo continuously.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> Never delete WAL or <code>pg_control</code> by hand to \"free space\"; that is a one-way door to an unrecoverable cluster. Never disable <code>fsync</code> outside throwaway systems.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Reconstructing a damaged ledger from the last audited page plus the receipts book entries since.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Believing recovery rolls back uncommitted transactions with undo records.</li>\n<li>Thinking replicas are required for crash safety; WAL alone gives it.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"vacuum-dead-tuples-and-bloat","title":"VACUUM, dead tuples and bloat","html":"<p><strong>Because UPDATE and DELETE leave old row versions behind, VACUUM must later free them for reuse.</strong> It scans for tuples no running snapshot can see, marks their space reusable (it does NOT shrink the file normally), updates the visibility map (used by index-only scans) and the free space map, and freezes old xids.</p>\n<p><strong>Autovacuum</strong> runs this automatically when dead tuples exceed <code>autovacuum_vacuum_threshold (50) + autovacuum_vacuum_scale_factor (0.2) x rows</code>. For a 100M row table that is 20M dead rows before it triggers, too late; tune per table:</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">ALTER</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> TABLE</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> events </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">SET</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">  autovacuum_vacuum_scale_factor </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 0</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">.</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">01</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">  autovacuum_vacuum_cost_limit   </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 2000</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">,</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">  fillfactor </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 90</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">);</span></span></code></pre>\n<p><strong>Bloat</strong> is dead or free space the table cannot reuse efficiently, so it is bigger than its live data. Causes: vacuum falling behind, long transactions pinning the horizon, replication slots / standbys with <code>hot_standby_feedback</code>, and mass updates. Symptoms: table/index size growing while row count is flat, slower scans, poor cache use.</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">SELECT</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> relname, n_live_tup, n_dead_tup, last_autovacuum</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">FROM</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> pg_stat_user_tables </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">ORDER BY</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> n_dead_tup </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">DESC</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> LIMIT</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 5</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">;</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Recovering space: <code>VACUUM FULL</code> rewrites the table under ACCESS EXCLUSIVE (outage); prefer <code>pg_repack</code> (online) or <code>REINDEX CONCURRENTLY</code> for indexes.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 806.4 130\" width=\"806.4\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Vacuum frees space for reuse; only a rewrite shrinks the file\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M115.2 65 L171.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M115.2 65 L171.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M368 34 L424 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M368 34 L424 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M570.4 34 L626.4 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M570.4 34 L626.4 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M115.2 65 L171.2 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M115.2 65 L171.2 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M368 96 L424 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M368 96 L424 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"63.6\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Dead tuples</text><rect x=\"171.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"196.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"269.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Autovacuum</text><rect x=\"171.2\" y=\"74\" width=\"196.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"269.6\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">VACUUM FULL or pg_repack</text><rect x=\"424\" y=\"12\" width=\"146.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"497.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Free space reused</text><rect x=\"424\" y=\"74\" width=\"146.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"497.2\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Smaller file</text><rect x=\"626.4\" y=\"43\" width=\"168\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"710.4\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Table file same size</text></svg><figcaption>Vacuum frees space for reuse; only a rewrite shrinks the file</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Transaction ID wraparound.</strong> xids are 32-bit; after about 2 billion transactions old ones must be \"frozen\" or data would appear to jump into the future. Postgres forces aggressive anti-wraparound autovacuum near <code>autovacuum_freeze_max_age</code> (200M default). If it still falls behind, Postgres stops accepting writes to protect itself. Famous outages (for example, Sentry and Mailchimp-class write-stalls from wraparound are discussed in public postmortems) show the pattern: monitor <code>age(datfrozenxid)</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Heavy-update tables (queues, counters, sessions) bloat fastest. Teams move queues to a separate table or Redis, and use HOT updates plus lower fillfactor to reduce vacuum pressure.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Clearing used plates from tables so new guests can sit; the restaurant (file) does not get smaller, but it stops needing more tables.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Expecting plain VACUUM to return disk space to the OS.</li>\n<li>Turning autovacuum off \"because it uses I/O\".</li>\n<li>Ignoring <code>age(datfrozenxid)</code> monitoring.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"putting-numbers-together-a-sizing-walk-through","title":"Putting numbers together: a sizing walk-through","html":"<p><strong>Goal: estimate storage, memory and WAL for a 200M-row orders table at 1,000 writes/s.</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Row ~150 B including header: 200M x 150 B = 30 GB heap.</li>\n<li>4 indexes averaging 6 GB each = 24 GB. Total about 54 GB, plus 20 to 30% bloat headroom: provision ~70 GB.</li>\n<li>Working set: last 30 days is ~15% of rows, so ~8 GB hot heap plus ~4 GB hot index pages: <code>shared_buffers = 8GB</code> on a 32 GB box is comfortable.</li>\n<li>WAL: 1,000 writes/s x ~500 B (heap + index records, illustrative) = 0.5 MB/s, about 43 GB/day.</li>\n<li>Checkpoint: <code>checkpoint_timeout = 15min</code>, <code>max_wal_size = 8GB</code>.</li>\n<li>Vacuum: set scale factor 0.02 on this table so it runs when ~4M rows are dead.</li>\n</ol>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 865.9999999999999 68\" width=\"865.9999999999999\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Sizing chain from rows to disk\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M122.4 34 L178.4 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M122.4 34 L178.4 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;0.201;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M268.4 34 L324.4 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M268.4 34 L324.4 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;0.401;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M434.79999999999995 34 L490.79999999999995 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M434.79999999999995 34 L490.79999999999995 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;0.601;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M651.5999999999999 34 L707.5999999999999 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M651.5999999999999 34 L707.5999999999999 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;0.801;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"67.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Rows x width</text><rect x=\"178.4\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"223.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Heap size</text><rect x=\"324.4\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"379.59999999999997\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Plus indexes</text><rect x=\"490.79999999999995\" y=\"12\" width=\"160.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"571.1999999999999\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Plus bloat headroom</text><rect x=\"707.5999999999999\" y=\"12\" width=\"146.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"780.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Disk to provision</text></svg><figcaption>Sizing chain from rows to disk</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Instagram and Notion both published stories of Postgres tables hitting hundreds of GB where vacuum, index size and migrations became the limiting factors before raw CPU did, which pushed them to partition or shard.</p>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> Partitioning big tables by time (declarative partitioning) makes dropping old data an instant <code>DROP TABLE</code> rather than a vacuum-heavy <code>DELETE</code>; adding it later requires a data migration, so choose early for append-heavy data.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Planning a warehouse: items, shelves, aisles and a spare bay for growth.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Estimating only heap size and forgetting indexes and bloat.</li>\n<li>Deleting old rows with a huge DELETE instead of partition drops.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"summary","title":"Summary","html":"<ul>\n<li>Tables are heaps of 8 KB pages; a row is addressed by ctid (page, slot); big values go to TOAST.</li>\n<li>shared_buffers caches pages; the OS cache is a second layer; watch hit ratio and use <code>EXPLAIN (ANALYZE, BUFFERS)</code>.</li>\n<li>WAL is written and fsynced before commit returns; data pages are flushed lazily. Full-page images guard torn pages.</li>\n<li>Checkpoints bound recovery time; tune <code>checkpoint_timeout</code>, <code>max_wal_size</code>; many \"requested\" checkpoints means max_wal_size is too low.</li>\n<li>Crash recovery = redo from the last checkpoint; no undo needed because aborted rows are invisible.</li>\n<li>VACUUM reclaims dead tuples for reuse (not file shrink); tune autovacuum per hot table; watch long transactions, slots and xid age.</li>\n<li>Fix bloat with pg_repack or REINDEX CONCURRENTLY, not VACUUM FULL in production.</li>\n</ul>"}],"questions":[]}